 "sections": [
  {
   "kind": "text-images-slider",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Exterior Design",
   "intro": "The Nauta design firm has designed the proportions and circulation to create a true outdoor living space that is both structured and fluid.\nAt the aft, two configurations transform life on board:\nIn its open configuration, the platform becomes a natural extension of the cockpit. The sea is invited on board.\nIn the closed configuration, the aft seats create a more secure area that enables you to welcome more guests. This layout creates a new living space in the cockpit - especially while cruising - thanks to its additional seating close to the helmsman.\nA convivial place at anchor. Makes navigation safer.\nThe helm stations benefit from the advanced features introduced on the Oceanis 47 and Oceanis 52: Integrated seats and backrests, ergonomic consoles incorporating all the controls, and a motor throttle integrated in the console. Every manoeuvre becomes intuitive; every setting becomes instinctive.",
   "items": [],
   "images": [
    "https://www.beneteau.com/sites/default/files/2026-06/oceanis-exterieur-1.jpg",
